<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.14.1: Modeling Equations to Solve a Riddle</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00627</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.14.1: Modeling Equations to Solve a Riddle</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6c7f3a14-185f-4dc2-b748-4866b2a65b84</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00001">For questions 1 – 4, use the following scenario to use equations to solve a riddle:</para>
            <quote id="quote-00001">Here is a riddle: “I am thinking of two numbers that add up to 5.678. The
            difference between them is 9.876. What are the two numbers?”</quote>
          <para id="para-00003">Name any pair of numbers whose sum is 5.678.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <para id="para-00005">2 and 3.678</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">Name any pair of numbers whose difference is 9.876.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <para id="para-00008">10 and 0.124</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">The riddle can be represented with two equations. Write the equations.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <para id="para-00011">Let <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> represent the numbers: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5.678</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>9.876</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00012">Solve the riddle. Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <para id="para-00014">The two numbers are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>7.777</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2.099</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>Adding the two equations eliminates the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-variable and gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>15.554</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> or
              <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7.777</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
            <item>Substituting this <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-value into either equation gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2.099</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
            <item>Graphing the two equations gives two lines that intersect at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7.777</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2.099</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
          </list>
          
            <media alt="Graph of a system of two linear equations with one solution.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_16_02_01.svg"/>
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>
  </content>
